module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.the_replaced_route_is_the_replacement_s_miss_path

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data the_replaced_route_is_the_replacement_s_miss_path: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "the_replaced_route_is_the_replacement_s_miss_path" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "the replaced route is the replacement's miss path (X is scheduled for deletion, and Y's cache-miss, cold-start, first-run or not-yet-built arm resolves to X; every Y execution therefore executes X, the migration reports as progressing, and X's removal date is unreachable because nothing ever stops depending on it)",
    "THE INSTANCE, gunbc 2026-09-11, operator design-review ruling C1. The native v2 compiler's acquisition path — prepare_emitted_compiler in the v2-native route harness — answered 'the emitted compiler is not present' by running the v1 seed in-process to emit it, then building that. Read as one execution it is correct and honestly receipted: the seed is named, the receipt records it, and nothing is fabricated. Read as a migration it is the defect, because the arm is not a step in getting off the seed, it IS the seed's standing production role wearing the name of a fallback. Every miss re-derives from v1; a miss is the ordinary case for a compiler nobody has built yet; so the seed executes on every ordinary run of the route whose entire purpose is to retire it. ",
    "WHY IT IS NOT MERELY AN ABSORBING FALLBACK, which is the neighbouring class. absorbing_fallback widens an ANSWER when precision is unavailable, and its harm is that the deficit stops being counted. Here the answer is precise and the receipt is accurate; what widens is the LIFETIME of the thing being replaced. The harm is therefore not a lost signal but a lost terminus: DESIGN section 3's replacement-migration doctrine requires X's authority to end in one motion, and an X reachable from Y's miss path has no motion in which that can happen — Y is not a replacement at all, it is a cache in front of X. The tell is textual and cheap: a route named for the new producer whose not-present arm names the old one. ",
    "THE REMEDY IS A CONSTRUCTOR RULE, not a policy preference: the ancestry relation between producer and produced artifact must have no constructor by which the retired producer is reached on the recurring path, so a missing or unverified ancestor has nothing to resolve to except a typed refusal naming what it expected. v2.compiler.self_host.ancestry models exactly two arms — a one-time GenesisFromSeed carrying its own deletion trigger, and the recurring SucceedsNative(N) -> N+1 — and NativeAncestorAcquisition's missing and unverified arms carry no producer at all. A Bool such as used_seed would have recorded the same fact while leaving both routes writable on either value, which is the carrier-without-a-wall shape this class keeps reappearing as. ",
    "THE CEILING AND WHERE THIS INSTANCE SITS. The class is decidable and fully modelled at the relation grain, so its attainable ceiling is structural impossibility (rung 4): with no seed-reaching constructor on the recurring arm, the invalid state has no inhabitant. NativeAncestorAcquisition Missing and Unverified carry no producer, so the MODEL PATH is at rung 4. The HOST miss path currently evaluates acquire_native_ancestor and compile_entry_emission is unreachable from acquire_native_compiler — the replacement v2.compiler.self_host.ancestry native_route_acquisition_frontier named has landed in source. That absence is not rung 2: DESIGN section 4b rung 2 is a generated test, lens, or gate that exposes and blocks the invalid state while it remains writable. No such mechanism is enrolled over v1_compiler.cli_run.native_lane_runner's acquisition path (review 65906). claim_executor --v2-native-route is off the acceptance path (gunbc.rung_drop v2_native_route_off_the_merge_path) and currently refuses every acquire via ReadBackUnperformed, so it is neither a discriminating RED nor a positive control for this class. The host path therefore remains mitigatable (rung 1): a miss is a typed V2-NATIVE REFUSAL rather than a silent seed emit when that host runs, and compile_entry_emission remains writable there. The class's current rung is the minimum across in-scope paths, which is the host's rung 1. THE NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER (rung 1 to 2) is a generated test, lens, or gate on a real acceptance path that REDs when acquire_native_compiler or prepare_emitted_compiler reaches compile_entry_emission, plus an accepted positive control that a missing ancestor is NativeAncestorMissing with no seed emit. Putting --v2-native-route on the merge path, observing ReadBackReported, or deleting GenesisFromSeed (genesis_migration_deletion_trigger) does not retire this climb (review 64141). gunbc.native_ancestry_genesis_seed_growth (modeled host acquire) is a later climb toward the ceiling, not the rung-2 trigger. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
